ofile" menu item renders only when provided. \n - `ThreadView.swift` and `DiscussionDetailView.swift` (the two hosts, 4 interactive call sites): added `@State private var profileDestination: ProfileDestination?`, a `.navigationDestination(item: $profileDestination) { ProfileView(pubkey:) }`, and pass `onViewProfile: { profileDestination = .pubkey($0) }`. The non-interactive `focusedHeader` row (`.allowsHitTesting(false)`) was intentionally left unwired. \n - `ProfileDestination.swift`: added `Identifiable` conformance (stable `id`) — required by `.navigationDestination(item:)`. [...] ### Task 1 — Accessibility labels added (per feature area) \n  \n | Area | File | Labels/traits added | \n |---|---|---| \n | Capture | CapturePageView | 2 (Close, Reset zoom) | \n | Capture | BookScannerView | 1 (Cancel scan) | \n | Capture | BookPicker | 1 (Clear search) | \n | Podcast | MiniPlayerView | 3 (Now playing + isButton trait + hint, Play/Pause) | \n | Podcast | PodcastListeningView | 3 (Play/Pause, Playback position scrubber + trait + hint, Clip FAB) | \n | Podcast | WaveformTickRow | 1 (Seek hint) | \n | Comments | CommentRow | 1 (like-status combined label) | \n | Comments | CommentComposer | 1 (Send comment) | \n | Communities | ChatView | 1 (Cancel reply) | \n | Communities | RoomHomeView | 4 (Capture, Suggest, New discussion, Invite people) | \n | Communities | CreateRoomSheet | 2 (Remove cover, Choose a cover photo on the clear-label PhotosPicker) | \n | Communities | RoomInviteView | 3 (Clear search, isSelected trait, Remove <name>) | \n | Communities | RoomShareCard | 1 (Show/Hide QR code) | \n | Profile | ProfileView | 1 (banner tap → isButton + label + hint) | \n | Profile | EditProfileSheet | 1 (Remove banner) | \n | Settings | KeysView | 1 (Reveal/Hide secret key) | \n | Settings | MediaSettingsView | 1 (Add media server) | \n | Settings | NetworkSettingsView | 1 (Add relay) | \n | Article | ArticleReaderView | 2 (Article image, Cover image — both tap-to-fullscreen) | \n | Feedback | FeedbackThreadDetailView | 1 (Send reply) | \n  \n **Total: ~32 accessibility modifiers across 20 files.** Many priority controls (e.g. ChatView send, BookScannerView torch, RoomExplorer add, HighlightDetail share/add-to-room, WebReader toolbar, comments attachment) were already labeled by the prior agent and left untouched. I skipped elements whose visible `Text`/`Label` already conveys the action (SwiftUI derives labels from those) and decorative-only icons (toast/empty-state/thumbnail glyphs, chevrons inside text-labeled rows). [...] - `Session/AppSessionStore.swift:25` and `:28` — keychain nsec / bunker-URI save \n - `Features/Podcast/PodcastPlayerStore.swift:422` (position encode) and `:440` (position decode) \n - `Features/Podcast/WaveformExtractor.swift:187` — waveform cache read \n - `Features/Capture/CaptureStore.swift:118` (page crop) and `:322` (OCR recognizeLines) \n - `Features/Web/WebReaderView.swift:156` (bundled Readability.js read, + missing-resource log) and `:345` (highlight quote JSON encode) \n - `Core/RichText/NostrRichText.swift:607` — nostr event-tags JSON decode \n - `Features/Podcast/TranscriptParser.swift:169` — JSON transcript parse \n  \n Each keeps the identical fallback (return nil/[]/uncropped) and adds a `.error` log with context and an identifying key. I left genuinely-benign sites as `try?` (literal-pattern `NSRegularExpression`, `AttributedString` markdown fallbacks, network artwork/JS-probe fetches, `AVCaptureDeviceInput` in the protected BookScannerModel). `Generated/highlighter_core.swift` and the other agent's guard-based crash fixes were not altered (my edits to BookScannerView/CaptureStore are purely additive). [...] 🔍 ANALYSIS: The decisive core API findings were that the NMP facade (`HighlighterNmpApp`) exposes `decodeNostrEntity(input): NostrEntityRef?` and a suspend `resolveNostrEntity`, but there is NO `OpenHighlight(eventId)` action — so the real routing path is decode→`OpenComments("e", eventId,