0c7b6-151 | 2026-06-12T15:34:10Z | session:0c7b6c09-7d1f-4cb2-b178-1adf69cd09ef | RESULTS — chosen strategy: **hybrid (d)**, formalized as one `OpRunner` primitive: shared 2-thread tokio runtime, `OpDomain`-keyed in-flight registry with generation supersession + `AbortHandle`, a single `KernelMsg::OpResolved` variant, all state mutation staying on the actor thread (`apply_op_outcome`), 30 s worker-side deadlines, D6 toast/busy-flag error surfacing. Rejected: timeouts-only (proven insufficient by the 30 s account-create repro), and concurrent async handlers (breaks the exclusive `state.write()`-between-emits invariant). \n  \n NEXT — migration phases in the doc: Phase 0 (stall instrumentation + `block_on_local` wrapper + CI lint, 1–2 days), Phase 1 (top-10 wedge sites incl. all Class A, 4–6 days), Phase 2 (~24 publish helpers, 1.5–2 weeks), Phase 3 (`handle_core_delta` hardening), Phase 4 (fold nine legacy workers into `OpRunner`). Test strategy includes a deterministic dead-network harness — relay URLs are currently compile-time baked via `include_str!("relay_policy.json")` (`relays.rs:46-56`), so the design adds a `relay_policy_json` config seam plus a black-hole TCP listener and the framework's `nak serve` in-process relay precedent, with an account-creation regression test that fails on today's code by construction. \n  \n COMPLETED: Design document delivered; OpRunner hybrid strategy grounded in ADR-0040 precedent. [...] - **`OpRunner`** (in `ActorRuntimes`, the actor's `&mut` state — `ActorContext` is `&`-shared so `submit_op` couldn't live there): 2-worker `new_multi_thread` runtime, `in_flight: HashMap<OpDomain, InFlightOp>` (AbortHandle + started), `generations: HashMap<OpDomain, u64>`, `submit_op` (bump generation → abort prior → worker-side `tokio::time::timeout` → `KernelMsg::OpResolved`), `is_stale`, and `cancel_all`. `OpDomain`, `OpOutcome` (per-domain typed payloads mirroring today's results), single `KernelMsg::OpResolved { domain, generation, outcome