f54b4-14 | 2026-06-12T20:28:27Z | session:f54b4a16-dacb-41e6-b32f-b737d606254f | Root cause: under the `codegen-schema` feature, FFI-visible kernel types derive `schemars::JsonSchema`. My new `RelayStatus.info: Option<RelayInfoDoc>` field broke the build two ways: (a) `RelayInfoDoc` didn't derive `JsonSchema`, and (b) more fundamentally, the V6 Stage-1 Swift emitter (`crates/nmp-codegen/src/swift.rs`) renders **flat-record types only** — a nested `Option<RelayInfoDoc>` produces an `anyOf`/`$ref` schema it explicitly rejects as Stage-2/3 scope. \n  \n Fix (the architecturally correct one, not just silencing): I gated the field **out of the schema** with `#[cfg_attr(feature = "codegen-schema", schemars(skip))]` on `RelayStatus.info`, and did NOT add `JsonSchema` to `RelayInfoDoc`. This is sound because iOS consumes `info` through the `relay_diagnostics` projection — both the authoritative serde-JSON subtree and the `KRDG` typed FlatBuffers sidecar (`InfoRow`) I already added — **not** through the flat `KernelTypes.generated.swift` mirror. `serde` still serializes the field; only the JSON *schema* omits it. \n  \n **Regen diff scope: ZERO Swift types changed.** I ran the exact workflow recipe (`cargo run -p nmp-core --features codegen-schema --bin dump_projection_schemas | cargo run -p nmp-codegen -- gen swift`, no `--check`) — it rewrote `KernelTypes.generated.swift` byte-identically to what's checked in. No types appeared, disappeared, or changed shape (the skip means `RelayStatus`'s emitted shape is unchanged from master). Both `gen swift --check` and `gen typed-decoders --check` pass locally and the **Swift codegen drift job is now green on CI**.
